{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>בנו בער.</b> Like ״לְמַעְיְנוֹ מָיִם״ (Psalms 114). And from the fact that both of them were greater than their fathers — Balak son of Zippor: his father was his son in kingship, and Balaam was greater than his father in prophecy — he was a man of the peras-coin (Sanhedrin 105; Tanḥuma)." "<b>שתם העין.</b> His eye is gouged out and protrudes outward, and its socket appears open — and it is Mishnaic language, that one should examine and close it and press it (Avodah Zarah 69). And our Sages said: because he said ״וּמִסְפָּר אֶת רֹבַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — that the Holy One, blessed be He, sits and counts the quarters of Israel: when will the drop come from which the righteous man is born? — he said in his heart: Should one who is holy and whose ministers are holy look upon such things? And on account of this the eye of Balaam was blinded (Niddah 31). And there are those who interpret <b>שתם העין</b> — open of eye, as Onkelos renders; and from the fact that he said ״שְׁתֻם הָעָיִן״ and did not say שְׁתוּם הָעֵינַיִם, we learn that he was blind in one of his eyes (Sanhedrin 105)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:33.336248484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}